      "content": "TRANSFER INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "377a6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Students are advised to complete the lower-division coursework in this agreement prior to transfer. Additional Resources: See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. Visit our Sac State Apply page for more information about our campus! Visit the Admissions website for current transfer admission requirements. Connect with an Admissions Counselor .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! </strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Students are advised to complete the lower-division coursework in this agreement prior to transfer.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Additional Resources:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csus.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>University Catalog</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Sac State Apply</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> page for more information about our campus!</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit the </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/application-process/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions website</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for current transfer admission requirements. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Connect with an </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/connect-with-admissions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions Counselor</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. </span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "3b7a6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3f7a6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Effective Fall 2026, the Psychology program at Sacramento State is transitioning to a pre-major. Students interested in becoming Psychology majors must have successfully completed the following courses or an approved equivalent with a grade of \"C-\" or better: PSYC 2, CHAD 30/PSYC 3, PSYC 8, and PSYC 9. Students must have the pre-major courses completed (grades must be posted to their transcript) before acceptance to the Psychology major will be processed. In-progress courses will only be accepted for transfer students completing their ADT (Associate Degree for Transfer). This exception is only for ADTs in Psychology, not other subjects. The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Psychology is compatible with the B.S. in Psychology at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division coursework with a \"C\" or better. For additional information, please visit: Department of Psychology .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Effective Fall 2026, the Psychology program at Sacramento State is transitioning to a pre-major. Students interested in becoming Psychology majors must have successfully completed the following courses or an approved equivalent with a grade of \"C-\" or better: PSYC 2, CHAD 30/PSYC 3, PSYC 8, and PSYC 9. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students must have the pre-major courses completed (grades must be posted to their transcript) before acceptance to the Psychology major will be processed. In-progress courses will only be accepted for transfer students completing their ADT (Associate Degree for Transfer). This exception is only for ADTs in Psychology, not other subjects.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Psychology is compatible with the B.S. in Psychology at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division coursework with a \"C\" or better.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/social-sciences-interdisciplinary-studies/psychology/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Department of Psychology</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></li></ol>"
    }
  ],
